    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_a73bcd01",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: being_conjoined_isn_t_easy; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts two conjoined twins, likely from a real-life context, surrounded by microphones from various media outlets, suggesting a press conference or public appearance. The overlaid text 'being conjoined isn't easy' is presented in a sarcastic or mocking tone, implying that the experience of being conjoined is somehow trivial or burdensome. This framing is harmful because it reduces a complex, often physically and emotionally challenging medical condition to a joke or a punchline, potentially trivializing the lived experience of conjoined twins. While not explicitly targeting a protected group with hate, the meme's intent is to mock a vulnerable condition, which can be seen as insensitive and potentially damaging to the dignity of those who live with such conditions. The overall intent is to elicit humor through the juxtaposition of the serious reality of conjoined twins with the dismissive, sarcastic text, which can be interpreted as a form of ableist humor that diminishes the gravity of their situation.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_aa36c805"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
